## Third-party source retained in this repository

### Daggerfall Unity

`reference/dfu-spec/` contains 120 C# source files and one data file (`NameGen.txt`)
from Daggerfall Unity, retained as an executable specification. The corpus directory
holds 124 tracked files in total: those 121, the upstream MIT licence and the two
project-owned custody records (`PROVENANCE.md`, `CLASSIFICATION.md`). None of them is
compiled, linked or copied into any product crate.

Copyright (c) 2009-2023 Daggerfall Workshop
Licensed under the MIT License.

Upstream: https://github.com/Interkarma/daggerfall-unity
Pinned release: v1.1.1
Pinned commit: 0038a1e61999ad2c73fb1f33b706cae9a88ec66f
Upstream license: https://github.com/Interkarma/daggerfall-unity/blob/v1.1.1/LICENSE

Provenance is mixed and is declared exactly in
`reference/dfu-spec/CLASSIFICATION.md`: **112 files** were taken at commit
`2343305d1d83ccc0de57a81e3b1e61188a997e34` and **9 files** (8 `.cs` plus
`NameGen.txt`) at `0038a1e61999ad2c73fb1f33b706cae9a88ec66f` — 121 upstream files
in total. Per-file SHA-256 hashes are listed in `reference/dfu-spec/PROVENANCE.md`.

`reference/dfu-spec/Assets/Resources/NameGen.txt` is retained byte-identical to
upstream (its file SHA-256 matches the DFU original). Its content is a name
model derived from the game's `NAMEGEN.DAT`; it is included here **as part of the
MIT-licensed DFU corpus**, not as an original work of this project.

The 62 region names in `crates/parser-bevy-bridge/src/npc_spec.rs` are
reproduced from the same MIT corpus
(`reference/dfu-spec/Assets/Scripts/API/MapsFile.cs`). No additional game bytes
are added by this project.

The full MIT text for this corpus is preserved verbatim at
`reference/dfu-spec/LICENSE.txt`. Provenance and per-file SHA-256 hashes are recorded in
`reference/dfu-spec/PROVENANCE.md` and
`reference/dfu-spec/CLASSIFICATION.md`.

